{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 56,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD, Keep ye judgment, and do justice: for my salvation ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " near to come, and my righteousness to be revealed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doeth this, and the son of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " layeth hold on it; that keepeth the sabbath from profaning it, and keepeth his hand from doing any evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to the LORD, speak, saying, The LORD hath utterly separated me from his people: neither let the eunuch say, Behold, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a dry tree.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thus saith the LORD to the eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and choose ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that please me, and take hold of my covenant;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even to them will I give in my house and within my walls a place and a name better than of sons and of daughters: I will give them an everlasting name, that shall not be cut off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to the LORD, to serve him, and to love the name of the LORD, to be his servants, every one that keepeth the sabbath from profaning it, and taketh hold of my covenant;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even them will I bring to my holy mountain, and make them joyful in my house of prayer: their burnt-offerings and their sacrifices ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " accepted upon my altar; for my house shall be called a house of prayer for all people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Lord GOD who gathereth the outcasts of Israel, Yet will I gather ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "others",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to him, besides those that are gathered to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All ye beasts of the field, come to devour, yes, all ye beasts in the forest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His watchmen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " blind: they are all ignorant, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all dumb dogs, they cannot bark; sleeping, lying down, loving to slumber.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " greedy dogs ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " can never have enough, and they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shepherds ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cannot understand: they all look to their own way, every one for his gain, from his quarter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.56.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.56.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come ye, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "say they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I will bring wine, and we will fill ourselves with strong drink; and to-morrow shall be as this day, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " much more abundant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
